@startuml 09-email
!include _style.iuml
title E-mail — the cards of a briefing sent, and the copy of an e-mail sent before

class EndUser
class "Anyone with the link" as Receiver
package "Presentation" {
    class briefingRouter {
        + GET /briefing/:id/stories/:storyId/pictures
        + POST /briefing/:id/news
        + DELETE /briefing/:id/news/:storyId
        + POST /briefing/:id/email
    }
    class mailRouter {
        + GET /mails/:token
    }
    class briefingController {
        + latest()
        + pictures()
        + importNews()
        + removeNews()
        + email()
        + original()
    }
}
note left of briefingRouter
    Each route for the administrators only
    (MAIL_REFUSED, 403). The e-mail: 10 an
    hour per IP address, 30 a day per reader;
    its body up to 9 MB (app.js), the files
    of the reader in base64
end note
note right of mailRouter
    No account: 60 reads in 15 minutes per IP
    address. The page runs nothing (CSP
    without scripts, sandbox), is not
    indexed nor framed
end note
package "Business" {
    class briefingService {
        + pictures()
        + importNews()
        + removeNews()
        + email()
        + withOwnTitles()
        + withoutTakenOut()
        + original()
    }
    class cardAnalysis <<other feature>> {
        + analysesOf()
    }
    class officialSources <<other feature>> {
        + officialSourcesOf()
    }
}
note right of briefingService
    The cards ticked, in the order of the reader,
    with the titles they wrote, without the lines
    they took out. Sent to another address: no
    "why" of the cards, the answers to the reader
    (Reply-To). No copy is kept since 13.10.2026.
    The cards sent are marked: left out of the
    next briefings for 48 hours (repeats.js)
end note
note bottom of cardAnalysis
    Written with the briefing (08-briefing),
    stored on it: the e-mail lays out
    what they found, in boxes of their own
end note
package "Data" as Data {
    class briefingModel {
        + ofUser()
        + articlePictures()
        + addItem()
        + removeItem()
        + markSent()
    }
    class userModel {
        + email()
        + roleName()
    }
    class profileModel {
        + get()
    }
    class sentMailModel {
        + byToken()
    }
}
package "Guards" as Guards {
    class jwt {
        + authenticateToken()
    }
    class admin {
        + adminOnly()
        + isAdmin()
    }
    class rateLimit {
        + rateLimit()
    }
}
package "Writing the e-mail" as Writing {
    class accountRules {
        + isEmail()
    }
    class mailPictures {
        + storyPictures()
        + withChosenPictures()
    }
    class publicUrl {
        + assertPublicUrl()
    }
    class briefingMail {
        + MAIL_FORMATS
        + briefingMail()
    }
}
note bottom of mailPictures
    Per card: taken out, an address of the
    web, or a file of the reader joined (cid:),
    JPEG, PNG, GIF or WebP told by its first
    bytes, 2 MB each, 6 MB per e-mail
end note
note bottom of briefingMail
    The page as a table with inline styles,
    its colours and fonts, dark where the
    mail app follows the system. The sentences
    as key points, a summary or key passages,
    the AI version of a card when asked
end note
class mailer {
    + mailEnabled()
    + sendMail()
}
class "SMTP account (Gmail)" as Smtp <<external>>
class "PostgreSQL" as PostgreSQL <<external>>

EndUser --> briefingRouter
Receiver --> mailRouter
briefingRouter --> Guards
mailRouter --> Guards
briefingRouter --> briefingController
mailRouter --> briefingController
briefingController --> briefingService
briefingService --> Writing
briefingService --> mailer
briefingService ..> cardAnalysis : reads what they stored
briefingService ..> officialSources
briefingService --> Data
mailPictures --> publicUrl
mailer --> Smtp
Data --> PostgreSQL
@enduml
